.TH AR86 1
.SH NAME
ar86 \- archive and library maintainer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ar86
key [\ posname\ ] archive [\ file\ ...\ ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ar86
keeps a group of files together in a single file, an
.IR archive .
Its main use is to make and update libraries of object files, from which
.BR ld86 (1)
takes the members a program needs:
.B "cc prog.c libutil.a"
links with one. An archive begins with the string
.BR !<arch> ,
and each member with a header of 60 characters giving its name, date,
owner, group, mode and size.
.PP
.I key
is a single letter for the operation, from among
.BR drqtpmx ,
and any number of the letters
.B abciluov
that change how it is done. The operations are:
.TP 6
.B r
Replace the named files in the archive, adding at the end any that are
not there yet (or at the place
.BR a ,
.B b
or
.B i
says). The archive is created if it does not exist.
.TP
.B q
Quickly append the named files to the end of the archive, without
looking for them in it.
.TP
.B d
Delete the named files from the archive.
.TP
.B t
Print a table of the contents of the archive: the named files, or all.
.TP
.B p
Print the named files, or all, to the standard output.
.TP
.B m
Move the named files to the end of the archive (or to the place
.BR a ,
.B b
or
.B i
says).
.TP
.B x
Extract the named files, or all; the archive is not changed.
.PP
The letters that change them are:
.TP 6
.B v
Verbose: give a line for each file the operation acts on. With
.BR t ,
give a long listing: the mode, owner, group, size and date of each
member.
.TP
.B c
Do not report that the archive is being created.
.TP
.B u
With
.BR r ,
replace only files newer than the members of the same name.
.TP
.B a
Put new or moved files after the member
.IR posname .
.TP
.BR b ", " i
Put new or moved files before the member
.IR posname .
.TP
.B o
With
.BR x ,
give the extracted files the dates of the members, not the present.
.TP
.B l
Accepted, and ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
	ar86 rv libutil.a strsave.o error.o	make or update a library
	ar86 t libutil.a			list what is in it
	ar86 x libutil.a error.o		extract a member
	ar86 d libutil.a error.o		delete it
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP 20
\fIarchive\fP_supersede
the new archive, while it is written, in the archive's directory (t_\fIarchive\fP
when the archive's name is long)
.SH SEE ALSO
ld86(1), cc(1), make(1), nm(1), size(1)
.SH HISTORY
An
.B ar
command first appeared in Version 1 AT&T UNIX.
.SH AUTHORS
ar86 is the ar of the GNU project, adapted for the 8086 tools by Greg
Haerr.
.SH BUGS
Member names are kept to 15 characters.
.PP
Do not use the
.B s
letter: the symbol index it writes is for another object file format,
and ld86, which reads every member, needs none.
